    Add generated editorial imagery: home hero, mission, flagship projects, volunteers (#21)

    Closes #20. Five duotone night/gold-graded photographs (generated,
    anonymous — no named team/board member is depicted) wired into five new
    optional CMS fields: home.heroImage, about.mission.image,
    projects.items[third-eye-kit/third-eye-world].image, volunteers.heroImage.

    Home hero image flows through the pre-existing --hero-image wiring
    (subtle underlayer beneath the ripple field, by the home redesign's
    original intent). About mission gets a framed photo beside the Rumi
    pull-quote. Third Eye Kit and Third Eye World project detail pages get
    full-bleed photo heroes with a night gradient for legibility, mirroring
    the home/volunteers treatment. Volunteers gets a new page-hero--photo
    variant (coexists with the existing page-hero--ripple modifier, also used
    by /donate, untouched).

    All new fields are optional casts guarded by isSafeImageUrl — clearing
    any of them in the CMS reverts that section to its pre-imagery look with
    no code change needed. Typecheck clean; 75/75 frontend tests pass; every
    placement verified live in the browser.


    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNuidX4hTo1eMcGoRyxZ8o

    Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

