## Critical correction first

**The imagery from commit `1be40b0` no longer exists in the current codebase.** The very next commit, `2a1e0c3` ("Revert Sight Beyond Sight redesign back to pre-session state"), reverted `90b31a7..1be40b0` in one changeset — the entire night-first redesign *and* the generated-imagery PR. Current HEAD (`751a900`) has none of: `home.heroImage` field, `about.mission.image`, `projects.items[].image`, `volunteers.heroImage`, `pd-hero--photo`/`page-hero--photo` CSS, or the `/images/generated/*.jpg` files (directory doesn't exist). `isSafeImageUrl` survived only because it predates that redesign and is used by three *other*, still-live components: `StoryCard.tsx`, `TeamCard.tsx`, `PhotoTile.tsx`. Those are the real current wiring examples, not the reverted ones.

**`isSafeImageUrl`** — `frontend/lib/utils.ts:25`:
```ts
const ALLOWED_IMG_ORIGINS = ['https://images.unsplash.com', 'https://www.thirdeyeworldwide.org', 'https://thirdeyeworldwide.org'];
export function isSafeImageUrl(url: string | undefined | null): boolean {
  if (!url) return false;
  if (url.startsWith('/') && !url.startsWith('//')) return true; // relative = same-origin, safe
  try {
    const { origin, protocol } = new URL(url);
    if (protocol !== 'https:' && protocol !== 'http:') return false;
    return ALLOWED_IMG_ORIGINS.includes(origin);
  } catch { return false; }
}
```
**Real current wiring example** (`frontend/components/media/PhotoTile.tsx:36-61`): `const safeImg = isSafeImageUrl(img) ? img : '';` then `{safeImg ? <div className="ph-img-bg" style={{backgroundImage:`url('${safeImg}')`}}/> : <div className="ph-placeholder"><ImageSquare/></div>}` — optional field, graceful icon fallback, same pattern the old mission/project code used.

## Checklist — field path → missing → subject → aspect ratio

- [ ] `home.heroImage` (empty in seed.json) → falls back to hardcoded generic Unsplash in `globals.css:215` (`.hero-photo`) → night establishing shot, person navigating/listening → full-bleed cover, ~2400×1350 (16:9, crops wider on desktop)
- [ ] `about.mission.image` (field doesn't exist; page.tsx has no `image` in `MissionContent`) → hands/braille or anonymous portrait beside the Rumi quote in `.about-visual` → no CSS class defined now, target ~4:5 or 1:1 (matches `.team-photo`/`.fs-quote-panel`)
- [ ] `projects.items[].image` — **none of the 5 items** (`third-eye-kit`, `te-voice`, `third-eye-ai`, `third-eye-world`, `third-eye-university`) have this field currently → prioritize `third-eye-kit` (hardware/wearer) and `third-eye-world` (voice-first community) as PR #21 did → no `pd-hero--photo` CSS exists now, would need re-adding; suggest full-bleed w/ night gradient, ~21:9
- [ ] `documents.blogs[]` (`eye-of-the-heart`, `third-eye-kit`, `third-eye-kit-v2`) → confirmed no `image` field, `DocCard.tsx` (line 49) renders only `.doc-hero {type}` gradient + text, zero image branching → editorial photos per report theme → `.doc-hero` aspect-ratio **16/10** (featured **16/9**)
- [ ] `documents.stories[]` visible items `s-open-call`, `s-founder-series` → `img: ""` → gradient-only via `StoryCard.tsx` → generic open-call/memoir imagery → 16/10
- [ ] Home "Latest Stories" grid (`page.tsx:72`, `[stories[0], blogs[0], stories[1]]`) → all 3 currently render imageless because the feeding items above are empty
- [ ] `media.photos[]` (p1–p10) → **all 10** use generic Unsplash stock URLs, strongest replace candidates → subjects already captioned (longboarder, cane commute, pianist, braille reader, etc.) → varied grid cells, aspect ~3:2 to 3:1 (`p-6-4`/`p-4-4` spans 2 rows ×180px, `p-3-2`/`p-4-2`/`p-6-2` span 1 row)
- [ ] `media.videos[]` (v1–v4) → gradient classes only, no thumbnail field, empty `youtubeId` → 16/9 (`.video-thumb`)
- [ ] `media.podcasts[]` → empty array; `.pod-art-bg` gradient square only → 1/1 if art added

Skipped: `about.board[]` (initials-only avatars by design, all `visible:false`) and the 4 `visible:false` Unsplash stories — out of scope unless re-enabled.
